on":"demote","note":"Nothing company-specific to size against the $680M cap."}]},{"case_id":"S12","class":"guidance_cut_inside_beat","passed":true,"verdict":{"grade":"routine","tier":"none","direction_vs_floor":"demote","materiality_tier":"material","fire_axes":[],"confidence":0.82},"failed_predicates":[],"rationale":"The quarter was a modest 3% revenue beat, but the same release cut full-year revenue guidance by about 8% at the midpoint ($610M to $562.5M) because enterprise sales cycles are getting longer. That is a deteriorating forward trajectory, the opposite of the beat-and-raise that growth names are paid for. The 'record quarter' headline is promotional framing, so the 8.9% gap is not backed by a positiv","axis_reads":[{"axis":"catalyst","lit":false,"direction":"demote","note":"Fresh, primary-sourced 8-K, but the net read is negative: a small beat against a large guidance cut."},{"axis":"materiality","lit":true,"direction":"demote","note":"Removing ~$48M from FY revenue guidance is material for a $2.4B company, in the negative direction."},{"axis":"gap","lit":true,"direction":"hold","note":"8.9% gap on 5.8x RVOL conflicts with the fundamentals and may fade."},{"axis":"theme","lit":false,"direction":"hold","note":"Not in an active theme."},{"axis":"narrative","lit":false,"direction":"hold","note":"Not in a narrative cohort; the 'record' headline is spin."}]},{"case_id":"S13","class":"guidance_cut_inside_beat","passed":true,"verdict":{"grade":"routine","tier":"none","direction_vs_floor":"demote","materiality_tier":"minor","fire_axes":[],"confidence":0.82},"failed_predicates":[],"rationale":"The EPS beat ($0.41 vs $0.29) comes from a 14% opex cut after January's restructuring, not from demand. Revenue of $96M missed the $103M consensus and fell 2% Y/Y, and the reaffirmed guidance implies a Q4 slowdown. Per the rubric this is a cost-driven EPS beat on a shrinking-revenue name, not a sustainable growth or turnaround inflection, so the gap and RVOL do not justify H