":"theme","lit":false,"direction":"hold","note":"Not in an active theme."},{"axis":"narrative","lit":false,"direction":"hold","note":"Not in a narrative cohort."}]},{"case_id":"S20","class":"unconfirmable_underlying","passed":true,"verdict":{"grade":"routine","tier":"MODERATE","direction_vs_floor":"demote","materiality_tier":"minor","fire_axes":[],"confidence":null},"failed_predicates":[],"rationale":"The only driver is a numberless 'record quarter / strongest bookings' claim from the IR page and a CEO social post, with no 8-K, earnings release, or wire item. No revenue, bookings, or margin figures exist, and the formal report is three weeks out, so the catalyst is unverifiable. The gap with 10.4x RVOL shows the market is voting, but without a verifiable fresh driver this caps at MODERATE.","axis_reads":[{"axis":"catalyst","lit":false,"direction":"demote","note":"CEO and IR claim with no figures and no 8-K or wire; real report is 3 weeks away."},{"axis":"materiality","lit":false,"direction":"demote","note":"Materiality cannot be assessed because no bookings or revenue numbers were given."},{"axis":"gap","lit":true,"direction":"hold","note":"15.3% gap with 10.4x RVOL at the 95th volume percentile is a strong market vote but not sufficient alone."},{"axis":"theme","lit":false,"direction":"hold","note":"Not in an active theme."},{"axis":"narrative","lit":false,"direction":"hold","note":"Not in a narrative cohort."}]},{"case_id":"S21","class":"strong_print_no_heat","passed":true,"verdict":{"grade":"routine","tier":"MODERATE","direction_vs_floor":"demote","materiality_tier":"minor","fire_axes":["catalyst"],"confidence":0.8},"failed_predicates":[],"rationale":"The catalyst is fresh and primary-sourced: the 8-K was filed premarket. It is a steady-state beat, with 9% Y/Y revenue growth, a 6% EPS beat and guidance only nudged to the upper half of the prior range, which is not a raise or an acceleration. There is no theme or narrative tailwind, so the 7.4% gap on 3.8 RVOL is a solid-print reaction rather than an episodic re-rating; this warrants MODERATE, n","axis_reads":[{"axis":"catalyst","lit":true,"direction":"demote","note":"Fresh 8-K beat; revenue +9% Y/Y, guidance only moved to the upper half of the existing range."},{"axis":"theme","lit":false,"direction":"hold","note":"Not in any active theme."},{"axis":"narrative","lit":false,"direction":"hold","note":"No narrative cohort; coverage calls it steady demand."},{"axis":"materiality","lit":true,"direction":"demote","note":"Incremental for an $8B company; no transformative element."},{"axis":"gap","lit":true,"direction":"hold","note":"7.4% gap on 3.8 RVOL is a real vote but modest."}]},{"case_id":"S22","class":"sympathy_no_own_catalyst","passed":true,"verdict":{"grade":"routine","tier":"none","direction_vs_floor":"demote","materiality_tier":"immaterial","fire_axes":[],"confidence":0.92},"failed_predicates":[],"rationale":"Every feed shows the move is pure squeeze mechanics: roughly 42% of float sold short, high borrow fees and social-forum momentum. There is no company news, filing, analyst action or corporate event today or this week. The last disclosure was a routine 10-Q five weeks ago. Under the rubric, a gap plus volume with no concrete company event is routine, so the floor's HIGH/strong verdict cannot stand.","axis_reads":[{"axis":"catalyst","lit":false,"direction":"demote","note":"No company event; the last filing was a routine 10-Q five weeks ago."},{"axis":"theme","lit":false,"direction":"hold","note":"Not in an active theme."},{"axis":"narrative","lit":false,"direction":"hold","note":"Not in a narrative cohort; only social-forum squeeze chatter."},{"axis":"gap","lit":true,"direction":"hold","note":"A 28.6% gap on 24.7x relative volume is the market's vote only, not sufficient on its own."},{"axis":"materiality","lit":false,"direction":"demote","note":"Nothing to measure against the $220M market cap."}]},{"case_id":"S23","class":"structural_upgrade","passed":true,"verdict":{"grade":"game_changer","tier":"HIGH","direction_vs_floor":"promote","materiality_tier":"transformative","fire_axes":["catalyst","theme"],"confidence":0.9},"failed_predicates":[],"rationale":"BIOA received FDA approval for its first product, a full-population label in moderate-to-severe atopic dermatitis, a large market. The approval is confirmed by an 8-K and a press release dated today, and launch is guided within 60 days through an established partner. For a $900M pre-revenue company this flips it to commercial stage, and the 24.8% gap on 18x RVOL in an active theme confirms the mov","axis_reads":[{"axis":"catalyst","lit":true,"direction":"promote","note":"First FDA approval with a full label and launch in 60 days; 8-K dated today."},{"axis":"materiality","lit":true,"direction":"promote","note":"Pre-revenue to commercial stage at a $900M cap; ratio flagged transformative."},{"axis":"theme","lit":true,"direction":"promote","note":"In active Lane 1 theme."},{"axis":"narrative","lit":false,"direction":"hold","note":"Not in narrative cohort."},{"axis":"gap","lit":true,"direction":"hold","note":"24.8% gap on 18.2 RVOL at the 99th volume percentile confirms but does not decide."}]},{"case_id":"S24","class":"structural_upgrade","passed":true,"verdict":{"grade":"game_changer","tier":"HIGH","direction_vs_floor":"hold","materiality_tier":"transformative","fire_axes":["catalyst","theme","narrative"],"confidence":0.82},"failed_predicates":[],"rationale":"The OCC granted final approval for a national trust-bank charter. The approval letter is dated yesterday and was confirmed by an 8-K filed this morning, so the catalyst is fresh and primary-sourced. This is a government/regulatory catalyst that structurally opens new regulated custody revenue lines, which is a re-rating event even for a $12B company. A hot digital-asset theme, narrative cohort mem","axis_reads":[{"axis":"catalyst","lit":true,"direction":"hold","note":"OCC charter approval dated yesterday, confirmed by an 8-